WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:02.585
- There has never been a
low of me wearing a shoe.

00:00:02.585 --> 00:00:03.712
There's never been
a worry about,

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:05.255
“Oh, I stepped my
shoe in the mud,”

00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:07.674
or “I spilled a fruit
punch, you know, on my shoes,”

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.134
or whatever the case may be.

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:10.844
I've never been
that type of person.

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:11.970
Shoes are meant to be worn.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.389
They supposed to have they own
lives and they own stories.

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:17.142
♪♪♪

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:19.602
♪♪♪

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:22.313
If I could think of any other shoe
that has amazing significance,

00:00:22.313 --> 00:00:23.940
I've always loved WWE.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.026
I was a big John Cena fan.

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:29.779
And I remember he was wearing
these shoes that pump up.

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:32.407
And I was like, “Man, what
shoe he keep pumping up?

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:34.284
And then he goin’
and hit someone

00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:35.577
with the Attitude Adjustment with.”

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:38.163
We ain't have no money, I mean,

00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:40.540
and making ends meet week by
week was already hard enough.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.126
Now you got me
saying, “Hey, Dad, you know, I

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:45.378
think I could get my basketball
game to the next level

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.047
if you put the right
shoes on my feet.”

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.465
And it was my
birthday coming up.

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:49.090
I was like, “You know what?

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:51.259
For my birthday, I don't
want nothing else but just

00:00:51.259 --> 00:00:52.510
these pumps.”

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.055
Man, he found a
way to get me them.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.556
I remember he
worked some overtime

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.515
and got me those shoes.

00:00:57.515 --> 00:00:59.142
My dad already worked six jobs.

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:02.103
So the fact that he had to do
overtime on top of the six jobs

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:04.355
shows you the commitment
he did to get me the shoes.

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:07.150
And man, I was pumpin’
them things everywhere.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.526
I walked outside, pump.

00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:10.445
Mom says something, pump.

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:11.488
Was on the court, pump.

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:12.614
Score a basket, pump.

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:13.948
Celebration.

00:01:13.948 --> 00:01:15.575
Like, I had it all goin’
with the pump.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.368
And those pumps have
a great story with me.

00:01:17.368 --> 00:01:19.579
They have a great time
in my life as well.

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:23.249
This shoe, these
were playoff PEs.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.793
They were only made
for the playoffs.

00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:28.254
I designed it in a way where
the person wearing the shoe

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.548
would find motivation every
single day in wearing the shoe.

00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:32.467
And they may see something
different every day

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:35.178
that may give ‘em more
of a drive to keep going.

00:01:35.178 --> 00:01:38.056
You see a lot of
sayings that I thought

00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:41.101
of or I have been
told: Just breathe.

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.228
Be positive. Be you. Believe.

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:46.022
If I was a little kid and I was
playing the game of basketball,

00:01:46.022 --> 00:01:48.191
and maybe I'm not doing
as well as I wanted to do,

00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:49.651
that shoe could
give you a reminder

00:01:49.651 --> 00:01:51.778
just to breathe, enjoy
life, enjoy the moment.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:55.365
Enjoy the present cuz
the future is imagination

00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:57.033
and the past is
learning and a gift, so.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.743
I wanted to
create something more

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:01.412
of, like, a movement, a culture,
something that breeds

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:03.081
positivity and
great mental health.

00:02:05.041 --> 00:02:07.836
I think it's always about
telling the story of the shoe

00:02:07.836 --> 00:02:11.005
without having to physically
write the story out for people.

00:02:11.005 --> 00:02:13.216
I would wanna do something
that has materials

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:15.802
that come from
Dominican Republic.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.554
Doing something super
cool and different,

00:02:17.554 --> 00:02:19.764
like incorporating
cane sugar from DR

00:02:19.764 --> 00:02:23.101
into the sole and materials
that come from Africa

00:02:23.101 --> 00:02:25.770
and finding ways to
get some of the fabrics

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:28.314
for the shoes that could have
a resemblance of being back

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.149
to the motherland.

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.234
And I think the shoe should
have versatility, so maybe

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.987
like a mid, you know? Kind of like a
mid-feeling basketball shoe

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.698
or a lifestyle shoe where it
could go with the high feel.

00:02:36.698 --> 00:02:37.949
It could go with the low feel.

00:02:37.949 --> 00:02:39.742
If you wanted to
skateboard in it, you can.

00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:42.453
If you wanted to play basketball
at a high level in it, you can.

00:02:42.453 --> 00:02:43.872
There's a lotta work to do.

00:02:43.872 --> 00:02:47.292
But the actual execution
of it...you never know.

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:48.960
You gave me an idea.
Maybe I’ll start one.

